From 0fed357ec04fa3871a7c0e4e33ae1792713d02de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 02:00:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06939/11362] [outer-loop] verify tier-3 induction crash fix
 end-to-end with a real live-path run

Follow-on to f2f2763bd's E3AgentPolicy._world_model_candidates missing-import
fix. That fix was verified against a mocked repro at commit time but never
against a real live-path run: exp5587 (the prior HUD-mask cascade check)
built E3AgentPolicy with a large default explore_budget on well-charted
games, so it was never established that its clean run actually reached
_world_model_candidates via a genuine stall.

experiment_5588_tier3_induction_live_path_sanity_check.py forces a fast
tier-1 stall (explore_budget=6) against a real offline game (m0r0) using the
REAL default tier-3 proposer (LocalGGUFProposer, Qwen3.5-9B-MTP, real GPU
inference -- not mocked), then checks whether _induce_and_plan's stall
branch (the code path containing the fixed crash site) completes without an
exception.

Result: stall_attempt_reached=True, stall_attempt_crashed=False. The fixed
crash site was genuinely exercised via a real LLM induce() call and did not
crash. The induced engine was correctly rejected downstream by the
HIDDEN_STATE_GAME_IDS trust gate (heldout_accuracy=0.0, only 7 transitions
available from the tiny forced budget) -- a legitimate, principled skip, not
a masked crash.

Two things found and handled along the way:

1. The sanity check's own default proposer construction would have silently
   reused the conductor's own long-running gemma-4-12B-it server (parked on
   the same default port 8919) instead of the intended Qwen3.5-9B-MTP model
   -- LocalGGUFProposer has no model-identity check on port reuse. Pinned the
   proposer explicitly to the already-warm, correctly-loaded Qwen server on
   port 8920 instead, avoiding both the wrong-model risk and contention with
   the conductor's work.

2. The run's duration fell under adversarial_verify.py's 60s live_llm_inference
   floor (calibrated for a cold model load + full generation). Independently
   corroborated as genuine rather than a shortcut by timing a comparable
   codeonly-shaped completion directly against the same warm server outside
   this script (25.43s elapsed, 406 tokens, 16.28 tok/s, MTP
   draft_n_accepted=273/402) -- consistent with a pre-warmed server skipping
   the model-load time the floor assumes. Disclosed honestly
   (flagged_adversarial=true + a methodology_note citing the corroboration)
   rather than suppressed, per the Adversarial Artifact Verification
   discipline.

Also reverted an unrelated side effect: the forced tiny-transition-budget
run overwrote results/arc_e3/m0r0/world_model.py (a shared induction-scratch
file other processes read) with a degenerate low-quality engine; restored
the pre-existing richer induced model before committing.

Adds REQ-ARC-WMTE-5588 + two scenarios to
openspec/capabilities/arc-world-model-trust-energy/spec.md and a 5-test
suite (3 isolated via monkeypatch, 1 validating the BLOCKED-PRECONDITION
fail-closed path, 1 validating the checked-in real-run artifact).

